# The build context for docker/Dockerfile.
#
# An allow-list, not a deny-list. A checked-out working tree here is around 600 MB,
# almost all of it web/node_modules, .venv, .git and the built demo bundles under
# docs/ - none of which the image needs, and all of which would otherwise be sent to
# the daemon on every build. Naming what the build reads means a new directory at the
# repository root costs nothing until someone adds it here deliberately.
*

# What the wheel is built from.
!pyproject.toml
!hatch_build.py
!README.md
!LICENSE
!src

# The TypeScript panel: built in the `web` stage, bundled into the wheel.
!web

# The `test` stage runs these against a real libindi; the runtime image also ships
# examples/ so a driver can be tried without mounting anything.
!examples
!tests

# The entrypoint the runtime stage installs.
!docker

# Re-excluded from inside the directories above: build output and caches that the
# image produces for itself, and that would otherwise arrive built for macOS.
**/node_modules
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/*.egg-info
web/**/dist
src/indi_nexus/web/static/panel
